0041-mods-import-and-save-restore-keep-old-until-new.patch -- two more places that deleted the working copy before the new one was in (docs/REVIEW-TRIAGE-2026-11-19.md, finding 3.1, sibling sites).
Applied by scripts/build-app.sh to its copy of the C# snapshot (patch -p1, run in the project folder), after 0040; app/gameapp/ is not edited.
UNTESTED ON DEVICE: written without a C# compiler; only System.IO calls the files already use.
  * GameAppMods.cs Import: a mod of the same name was deleted, then its entries copied one by one, so a damaged zip entry in the middle destroyed the mod that worked. Now every mod is
    copied into games/<id>/mods.new (outside mods/: never listed, never read by a build), and only when all of it is there do the old folders go and the new ones move in.
  * GameAppSaves.cs ReplaceDir (save restore): the live save folder was deleted before the restored one moved in. It is now renamed to <folder>.old, the new one moves in, and a failure puts
    the old one back (the restore also takes a safety copy of the current save first, so this was never the only copy; it is now not even the only protection).
